          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"hamsun-victoria-70fda1fe7e4c1933\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.94,\"analysis\":\"Johannes directly avows that he loves Victoria and explicitly marks the present moment of disclosure. The utterance is chiefly truth-conditional. Its request for her answer gives it weak courtship or relationship-invoking force, but it does not clearly undertake a commitment in the narrower P sense. Despite intense emotion, the deliberate wording and structured request for an answer do not independently support expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"There is slight T/P ambiguity because the avowal functions within a bid for reciprocation, but courtship and anticipated relational consequences alone provide only weak evidence for P.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Johannes directly says “Jeg elsker Dem” to Victoria during an emotionally intense request for her answer.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Johannes’s confession culminates an extended, highly emotional declaration of admiration and hope. He says explicitly that he is declaring his love now, asks Victoria to answer, and presents himself as dependent upon her response. His immediate plea that she not answer reveals fear and vulnerability rather than changing the avowal’s core force. The surrounding confused outbursts and intoxication-like emotion establish intensity, but not a distinct reflex-like production of the highlighted words.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg elsker Dem og sier det nu.”\",\"supports\":\"A direct present avowal, with explicit metapragmatic awareness of making the disclosure now, strongly supports T and weighs against a reflex-like E reading.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Det vil da avhænge av Deres svar om jeg .... De råder så aldeles over mig. Hvad svarer De?”\",\"supports\":\"Johannes solicits Victoria’s response and makes future consequences depend upon it, supplying limited relationship-invoking pressure toward P.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After a pause Johannes lowers his head and begs, “Nei si det ikke!”\",\"supports\":\"His retraction of the request for an answer shows vulnerability and fear of rejection while leaving the preceding love avowal intact.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Earlier, “Hele hans sjæl strømmet imot hende,” and his attempted speech becomes “forvirrede utbrudd”; he is described as if intoxicated.\",\"supports\":\"The scene is intensely affective, but these delivery and framing cues alone do not show that the highlighted, deliberately announced confession has independent expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"confidence\":0.93}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the central avowal, while a low P score records its limited role in seeking relational reciprocation. Emotional intensity is adequately handled contextually without E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
      ],
